  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing User Intent**\n\nI\'m meticulously reviewing the user\'s recent input, particularly focusing on the stated priorities of Squad Building, Club Sync, and Evolution. I\'m carefully dissecting each detail to grasp the nuances and requirements provided. My aim is to extract the core needs and expectations to ensure a precise and tailored response.\n\n\n**Optimizing Sync Mechanisms**\n\nI\'m now prioritizing the automation of club data synchronization. Eliminating manual photo/video uploads is key. I\'m investigating compatibility with tools like EA Web App userscripts, FUT Enhancer, Antigravity, and Google Drive auto-sync for seamless data flow. I\'m also focusing on Evolution chaining recommendations based on the user\'s club and external market player suggestions.\n\n\n**Calculating Spending Strategies**\n\nI\'m now focused on financial resource allocation within the FIFA ecosystem, specifically coins and FIFA points. I\'m actively monitoring Squad Building Challenges (SBCs), noting their exact countdown, associated costs, and available fodder in the user\'s club. I\'m grounding all information to the current timestamp in British Standard Time and the 2026-27 season. I\'m also ensuring that information is current, and I\'m avoiding outdated player data.\n\n\n**Verifying Data Integrity**\n\nI\'m now prioritizing data accuracy, especially regarding player transfers and squad rosters for the 2026-27 season. I will cross-reference the data from FotMob and FUTBIN to ensure its validity. I\'m also researching open-source EA Sports FC tools on GitHub and comparing them to existing companion apps. This will inform the development of a comprehensive comparison matrix, highlighting our app\'s strengths, including personalized club sync and Evolution chaining. Furthermore, I will create a utility function to show the current time in British Time.\n\n\n**Establishing Time Context**\n\nI\'m now integrating a dynamic timestamp display (BST/GMT) and a \"T=0\" timer alongside contextual elements like the season (2026-27, First Half) and matchday events (e.g., UCL drops). This precise timestamp will be the anchor for all subsequent data retrievals and search queries. I will also incorporate a web search on GitHub, focusing on EA Sports FC 27 Ultimate Team Console to compare and contrast features with Futbin.\n\n\n"
