      title: "github.com"
    }
    summary: "The **Model Context Protocol (MCP)**[1] is an open standard created by Anthropic[1] that allows AI assistants (like Claude[1], Cursor[2], and other MCP clients[3]) to securely connect to external data sources, tools[1], and developer environments[4]. \n\nThe list of technologies you mentioned\342\200\224**SQLite, Postgres, Playwright, Fetch, Brave Search, Google Drive, and GitHub**\342\200\224represents some of the most popular and foundational **MCP servers** used to give AI models \"hands\" and direct data access[1].\n\n---\n\n### Overview of These Specific MCP Servers\n\n1. **SQLite (`@modelcontextprotocol/server-sqlite` or community variants)**\n   * **Purpose:** Connects the AI directly to local SQLite databases[5].\n   * **Capabilities:** Allows the LLM to inspect database schemas, write and execute SQL queries, analyze data tables, and perform lightweight business intelligence tasks locally[5].\n\n2. **PostgreSQL (`@modelcontextprotocol/server-postgres`)**\n   * **Purpose:** Connects securely to PostgreSQL databases (typically configured for read-only access by default for safety)[5].\n   * **Capabilities:** Enables the AI to explore table structures, query relational data, troubleshoot database schemas, and pull live operational data into the context window[5].\n\n3. **Playwright / Puppeteer (`@modelcontextprotocol/server-playwright` / `puppeteer`)**\n   * **Purpose:** Provides browser automation and web scraping capabilities[5][6].\n   * **Capabilities:** Enables the AI to open a real browser instance, navigate websites, click elements, fill out forms, and read structured accessibility snapshots or DOM content to interact with live web applications[6].\n\n4. **Fetch (`@modelcontextprotocol/server-fetch`)**\n   * **Purpose:** A lightweight utility server for retrieving raw web content[7].\n   * **Capabilities:** Allows the AI to pass specific URLs (such as API docs, raw text files, or specific GitHub release notes) and ingest the response body directly into its context for efficient parsing[7].\n\n5. **Brave Search (`@modelcontextprotocol/server-brave-search`)**\n   * **Purpose:** Grants the AI access to live internet search capabilities via the Brave Search API[8][9].\n   * **Capabilities:** Performs web and local business searches, allowing the agent to discover up-to-date URLs, documentation, or news that it can subsequently read[8][7][9].\n\n6. **Google Drive (`@modelcontextprotocol/server-google-drive`)**\n   * **Purpose:** Bridges your cloud storage documents directly to your AI assistant[5].\n   * **Capabilities:** Allows the AI to search for files, read Google Docs or spreadsheets, and pull context from your personal or enterprise Google Drive folders[5].\n\n7. **GitHub (`@modelcontextprotocol/server-github`)**\n   * **Purpose:** Integrates deeply with GitHub\'s platform (often maintained officially by GitHub or community leaders)[10][1].\n   * **Capabilities:** Gives the AI the ability to read repositories, inspect file contents, search code, manage issues, review pull requests, and check CI/CD pipeline statuses[10][1].\n\n---\n\n### How They Are Configured\nMCP servers are typically run locally via Node.js (`npx`), Python (`uv` / `pip`), or Docker containers, and are declared inside an MCP client configuration file (such as `claude_desktop_config.json`)[11][9]. \n\nFor example, a basic setup combining a couple of these servers looks like this:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"mcpServers\": {\n    \"sqlite\": {\n      \"command\": \"uvx\",\n      \"args\": [\"mcp-server-sqlite\", \"--db-path\", \"/path/to/database.db\"]\n    },\n    \"fetch\": {\n      \"command\": \"npx\",\n      \"args\": [\"@modelcontextprotocol/server-fetch\"]\n    },\n    \"brave-search\": {\n      \"command\": \"npx\",\n      \"args\": [\"@modelcontextprotocol/server-brave-search\"],\n      \"env\": {\n        \"BRAVE_API_KEY\": \"YOUR_API_KEY\"\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\nYou can discover hundreds of additional official and community-maintained servers through the **[Official MCP Registry](https://registry.modelcontextprotocol.io)** or repositories like `modelcontextprotocol/servers` on GitHub[12][11].\n\nSources:\n[1] [aibytec.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHWjs7WOQewYZ_PT0JNP8o9xce5k8jLRJv0MLtZc_th75hEcNoy-o00obXTsvT5jAytKhAxnSZtBNaGZGBI6nhLd2f3debMbm2FMCVHRF5lCpfXXVCtTBvu0wbklntOPgMvTpGHgpi9xGxtSOvqqsMZwaW8-lPEgOv3T3oDaFHrvmzAJA==)\n[2] [mcpservers.org](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGQyVImYbprZ-T2KuTvnN9y9SUv3GBrKGFZrqi00LlCAK0sy10FRf3a1HTRimFqmxP2DRcp9Eb5je0n2X2ezwmZfwbjQvF5iuEH7ZUO)\n[3] [mcp.so](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFJO8JyA2DOGzuqk3chFqBzGzwxzvWQ8_7hQ5wE3HhPnp94zmTxmCEl89NOJV3mzcu0ZwhpycMZm9w9KbSUblA7C5DwWw==)\n[4] [anthropic.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQF5vdrN6IQg1YnnOktOZaU-kzE-VI2zPe-jX29NKy-6RRXFGGCUqWtM1vJxBI-9ryZS0YrL4deGXdV7v8a1HPo4tDCytgBFvZbjbhBW0if02KYmUDj9SNAWLNv3n_B8NoMb-JZWKHa3WOAL)\n[5] [github.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGwQu9R_YuOa7xXW-wiDebr_FgME1dRCGB6tpCp_P9xw5-vWn7odOOISh4JgE2YZ01fri2mEIFECdF2eikmOdp0G8kDAMMzH52c7z7XI0DSRNlsndYdYG4S75G3QKE2Z_8UESU5)\n[6] [medium.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQE11wuH73B6yUt4rAyg_Aa8SyIpvV4bvfd-PxWNDREnjKkXMw5V6tXtO0TyPii6PUIfemMHOtLGNwc_g8u4hz9GjA9XQ3qEfAUSy7Zf0HVhcZz55WBJpOqHK_J2rRpkqXH8X-W3thxwrk0v-Yiy1YkXHX00mMrOLamDKytwHBC4NJf_N7nk0ULVlsLkAFSLQT_FwbbSVw7bDOLoV6wdpHS-pr9OwE_d)\n[7] [iamraghuveer.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQF35Inc3Ro6qTahYxaJcIgevPseR_r-ivAcXIJ2a-_r7CVRszEL6Ioh--W2CLATdW0iIenRbtV1OaZBX3WTwojvEU98BT0IKF3MTWXm0N5BBXuEVPquGUka9zKtn8Pr8SpXZ1-e_kdH6FiUR6Yoa5Jm6QCXfZ40)\n[8] [github.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFbQKAQPh5JQgDhjBdhNtIYakvGF0_u55jXe_QxdH6kbwRRRixep8LCE5DOH_c-WJPsvS-wEMQJO5QClMCwdk74vJ7mzrDiNNxBP5Y6yySD-bPrMOu7nvh1TJlKzvOMPpAn8ZaWjiX8WK4Zew==)\n[9] [mcpservers.org](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFjFx8r5euL01OCnUJLOYh5xc5KS4wfvxMmlQYSDNAMbMHBEUQx5T-pqzboRQqLcuFkZzH9qur5s4DuDfHijFSZbXv3dfdnHIeEYZECb1I7yeuWHm9FadozpLtZoEeq66g5YkGd6lQB9laNaqFRYw==)\n[10] [mcpverdict.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHD4lADgl927ik28cbTqGjMvcruOIak-uuSN--gBxajHdLz9MSAsEnDc3kRtEWfjSIGC6fAvevCD8XqHWzT2v5-qUxpNotDzX0xi8DIZD--14a5MFWC4nMx)\n[11] [modelcontextprotocol.info](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQF3vOaP7yT1AY3rPXA2gA6ZxgJkuIXileINRZZs0ubOUw9U484EA2tTW3d5Hq9BYijKiZzJ3CD04COKz-Esl4ui5PfDX4EAPsUnuhELNgyU0JdDWUZ96QZLuhK_6isS5lYvNEIfChU=)\n[12] [github.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGwQu9R_YuOa7xXW-wiDebr_FgME1dRCGB6tpCp_P9xw5-vWn7odOOISh4JgE2YZ01fri2mEIFECdF2eikmOdp0G8kDAMMzH52c7z7XI0DSRNlsndYdYG4S75G3QKE2Z_8UESU5)"
    third_party_config {
      provider: THIRD_PARTY_WEB_SEARCH_PROVIDER_GEMINI
    }
    search_type: SEARCH_WEB_TYPE_WEB
  }
}
