  planner_response {
    response: "I have updated the implementation plan to include the **6 recommended MCP (Model Context Protocol) Connectors** mapped directly to **FUTBIN FC 27 Console** and **FotMob (`2026\342\200\22327` Season)** resources for your Antigravity 2.24 and Asus ZenBook UX482 pipeline:\n\n1. **`playwright-futbin-mcp` (`@modelcontextprotocol/server-playwright`)** \342\200\224 Scrapes JS-rendered FUTBIN FC 27 console endpoints (`futbin.com/27/players`, **Market Index 100 / Rating Indices**, **FUT Gallery Sets & Tags**, hourly price graphs, and **PGP** stats) plus **FotMob** live `2026\342\200\22327` rosters.\n2. **`fetch-patch-sbc-mcp` (`@modelcontextprotocol/server-fetch` / `firecrawl-mcp`)** \342\200\224 High-speed ingestion of FUTBIN\'s **Cheapest by Rating** tables (`futbin.com/27/cheapest-by-rating`), **Active SBC Requirements**, **Evolutions**, and **EA FC 27 Title Update Pitch Notes** at the 18:00 BST daily drop.\n3. **`sqlite-fc27-cache-mcp` (`@modelcontextprotocol/server-sqlite`)** \342\200\224 Local SQLite cache (`fc27_futbin_mirror.db`) storing console prices, Holographic multipliers, 31 Roles++, and your synced Club Inventory so Dual-Mode SBC and Gameplay Synthesis math run in **<2ms with zero Gemini API quota waste**.\n4. **`memory-transfer-graph-mcp` (`@modelcontextprotocol/server-memory`)** \342\200\224 Persistent Knowledge Graph locking in verified `2026\342\200\22327` club transfers (e.g., Rodri at FC Barcelona) and your active Evolution chains to override LLM frequency bias.\n5. **`google-drive-workspace-mcp` (`@modelcontextprotocol/server-google-drive`)** \342\200\224 Automatically syncs exported EA Web App club JSON files (`Paletools` / `FUTClubAnalyzer`), SBC solutions, and daily drop snapshots with Google Drive.\n6. **`github-ut-tools-mcp` (`@modelcontextprotocol/server-github`)** \342\200\224 Monitors open-source FC 27 Web App exporter schemas (`FUTClubAnalyzer`, `AutoSBC`, `FC-Tracker`) for schema changes after EA patches.\n\nThe updated implementation plan is ready for your review."
