      title: "google.dev"
    }
    summary: "Recent updates to the **Google Antigravity IDE** (spanning versions **v2.24** through **v2.25**) bring significant architectural enhancements tailored for agent-first software engineering[1]. \n\n### Key Updates & Features in Versions 2.24 / 2.25\n\n* **Deep Integration with the \"Jetski\" Agent Platform:** \n  Version 2.25 introduces core structural logic linking the IDE to Google\'s internal *Jetski* agentic platform[1]. This includes native XML reasoning scaffolding (`<JETSKI_THOUGHT>`, `<JETSKI_USER>`, and `<JETSKI_OUTPUT>`) that exposes internal chain-of-thought scratchpads to track agent logic in real-time[1].\n* **Safety Classifiers & CoT Exploit Scanners:** \n  The language server components have been updated with active scanning on reasoning tags. If a background agent attempts an unintended exploit or risky system modification during a task, dedicated internal classifiers intercept the tool call before it impacts the host system[1].\n* **Browser Agent & Chrome DevTools MCP Integration:** \n  The environment features an upgraded browser subagent (invokable via commands like `/browser`) tightly coupled with native **Chrome DevTools Model Context Protocol (MCP)** integration[2]. This allows autonomous agents to inspect live web apps, run UI verification, interact with elements, and record sessions (such as WebM walkthroughs)[2].\n* **Model Context Protocol (MCP) Workspace Scaling:** \n  Antigravity\'s MCP implementation allows developers to connect external databases, APIs, and tools (such as BigQuery, Looker, GitHub, or custom services) directly to the workspace[3][4]. Workspace configurations can be handled globally or scoped via project paths (such as `.agents/mcp_config.json`) to give agents real-time context for local schemas, logs, and development tools[3][5].\n* **Expanded Model Routing:** \n  Updates across the v2.24\342\200\223v2.25 cycle hardcode and refine routing frameworks for advanced frontier models (including internal/experimental codenames like *ORIONFIRE*, *GENTLEISLAND*, etc.)[1] to manage multi-agent orchestration, parent-child subagent delegation, and background task loops more efficiently.\n\nSources:\n[1] [reddit.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQESQA41SHss2NaB5_iq37nMOfnKkcSmahTVr5EYUB0GQAm8aJ9foZCXcusUnx1NwiMQtApXGS6uN2d3XuPbeM5u_G06MwUHv7jWRQUm8vpKFIctGSWOdnl-nC0BbbCnMpmZgqR9kvUyU7zWKiOcRcoul-T71ZRcL9JDz7QIH_elOsHBHJiYuvNs3vjuaxg8a49qCG6uaAF4BaOr3IXzA6KAy5iwuTU=)\n[2] [antigravity.google](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGDzSvvrRZSNABiWYz9o0RzIr9qYNOKML4LgVXdvSZq3B-zofVjjGwPALEQruYkSJ1iYa2xyiNQxkq1Ppedp8pfQYIN0PPsNhdU1Xlp6l683pvKLxCCr5hUCs_JpRImlw==)\n[3] [antigravity.google](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFLOCZ5aaZCzWhr4PhyaI0bdphovTo3iN3dcnlpKt4OIAE0u-W8Gx9VnQyY3afgcQmyH_GFGOiUjnd50Zj1zhtQQ48VI0lRx1agLtjqkVjeFnOHIEJouol-Zto=)\n[4] [google.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGkxiq9XKJx0ituXd5RQ40Lz5eQ-1E8h-67petEyXKz9rvK6bqfrGQTq9UBFqBEYrd9ddOFMEHxKeGvQZgrRD3bDr8Fs9Iv3Rultc4wi-qVKN6yfBIysSE4ypinuBEkYHPtKBFKmATDELzga3LerA4cH_MbFmum-tiOAoy-dnZdFIkJDbMRX4OPlVUzNy9_pQ6WvvqnYKGTbgdkEXyv2M5DAM-cQswUslHZ)\n[5] [google.dev](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQExg2Urk3-A1WJmzk8l1nZWyuaVjMvn8U32OgiBIBMlRMkqt4gwPhBGZuj57M9Hz3qnifb2IcKjP8bB7H2xhUzDhExsjvBrXud811VKccIRN9POZVqGg-_USjc-H-AXNqSqgX7h_n_1rZqNAT8G7FEvy-06PM-xdmdWmja8S3uveD2qI4U0r_yVBlzTw4UhQ9Q=)"
