  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Installing Firebase Dependencies**\n\nI\'m currently focused on integrating Firebase into the project. The plan is to install the `firebase` package using `install_applet_package`, ensuring access to `firebase/app`, `firebase/auth`, and `firebase/firestore`. Concurrently, I need to update the `/metadata.json` description and `/index.html` title and meta tags to comply with the environment specifications. I\'m using `install_applet_package` to get started.\n\n\n**Refining Firebase Configuration**\n\nI\'m now diving deeper into the Firebase setup. I am simultaneously focusing on several files: `/metadata.json`, `/index.html`, `/firebase-blueprint.json`, `/security_spec.md`, and `/firestore.rules`. I\'m adhering strictly to the schema for `/firebase-blueprint.json` and developing `/security_spec.md`, which includes data invariants and the test runner. Additionally, I\'m working to create hardened `/firestore.rules` based on the 8 pillars. I\'ll deploy these rules using `rpc_action`. I\'m also planning the Firestore schema, considering a `/users/{userId}` collection with `UserClubState` entities.\n\n\n**Defining Firestore Entities**\n\nI\'m currently formalizing the Firestore entities. I\'m focusing on two main collections: `/users/{userId}` and `/users/{userId}/investments/{investmentId}`. For `/users/{userId}`, I\'m defining fields like `galleryLevel`, `activeFormation`, and timestamps for `createdAt` and `updatedAt`, ensuring data integrity. I\'m also specifying the `TrackedInvestment` entity for the nested collection, including fields such as `playerId`, `playerName`, `buyPrice`, `targetSellPrice` and the important constraints on `ownerId`.\n\n\n**Validating Firestore Data**\n\nI\'m now deeply engaged in validating the data for the `/users/{userId}/investments/{investmentId}` collection. I\'m focusing on the `TrackedInvestment` entity\'s fields: `number`, `quantity`, `status`, `createdAt`, and `updatedAt`. I\'m using the 8 Pillars of Hardened Rules. This entails validation for numbers within the specified ranges and an enum for the `status` field. Time is tracked for audit reasons. I\'ve designed functions such as `isValidId(userId)`, `isValidId(investmentId)`, `isValidUserClubState(data)`, and `isValidTrackedInvestment(data)` to ensure robust data integrity. I am now working on security around ownership to ensure a master gate.\n\n\n"
