  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Verifying UI Requirements**\n\nI\'m currently investigating whether the `show_aistudio_ui` function needs to be called with `\"paid_model_flow\"` due to the app\'s use of `gemini-4-argon`. To confirm this, I\'m reading `gemini-api/SKILL.md`, specifically lines 85-89, to determine if the model necessitates a specific UI flow.\n\n\n**Confirming UI Flow**\n\nI\'ve determined that a paid API key is necessary for the model, so I must prompt the user by calling `show_aistudio_ui` with the correct argument. Also, I\'ve checked the description of `show_aistudio_ui`, which clarifies that I must wait for the user\'s response after calling it. Now, I\'m shifting focus to frontend development. I\'m going to create all the frontend components, styling, and `App.tsx` first to ensure the application builds, compiles, and runs properly on port 3000. For modularity and maintainability, I\'m planning specific components such as custom font setup and a dark canvas theme.\n\n\n**Synthesizing Game Stats**\n\nI\'m now focusing on synthesizing in-game performance from isolated stats, comparing them side-by-side. I\'m also tracking the latest title updates, formations, and share codes. Furthermore, I\'m working on a 33/33 chemistry squad builder with a branching evolution simulator and planning to compare various ecosystem resources, like FUTBIN, FUT.GG, and our own app. Finally, I\'m integrating a multi-turn Gemini chatbot to support advanced reasoning and search grounding, and I am configuring the Antigravity 2.0 orchestrator.\n\n\n**Designing Dashboard Elements**\n\nI\'m now diving into the design of the dashboard elements, specifically the `/src/App.tsx` structure. The top bar will feature brand elements, navigation links, and Google Sign-In, along with a telemetry sub-header indicating British time, season details, and countdown information. A dual-domain switcher will facilitate navigation between menus (market, SBCs, club sync) and gameplay (squad builder, formations). I\'m also planning a secondary ticker mode for dual-screen laptops and a mobile bottom navigation bar, all culminating in cloud sync with a crucial confirmation dialog. I\'m focusing on `/src/index.css` next.\n\n\n"
