    user_requests: "Integrate an AI-driven recommendation engine into the EA Sports FC 27 Ultimate Team assistant app to provide solutions for Squad Building Challenges (SBCs). The AI should analyze the user\'s current player inventory, market prices, and SBC requirements to suggest the most efficient and cost-effective player combinations. Ensure all data is sourced from EA Sports FC 27 Ultimate Team console and recommendations are optimized for mobile display.\n\nIntegrate an AI-driven recommendation engine into the EA Sports FC 27 Ultimate Team assistant app to provide solutions for Squad Building Challenges (SBCs). The AI should analyze the user\'s current player inventory, market prices, and SBC requirements to suggest the most efficient and cost-effective player combinations. Ensure all data is sourced from EA Sports FC 27 Ultimate Team console and recommendations are optimized for mobile display.\n\nImplement a data synchronization feature for the EA Sports FC 27 Ultimate Team assistant app that seamlessly integrates with the user\'s game data. This includes syncing current coin balance, FIFA points, active in-game promotions, newly released players, active Evolutions, and available SBCs. The synchronization should be as real-time as possible and optimized for mobile viewing.\n[AIS_METADATA_SECTION_START]\nPlan action: revise\nPlan path: .aistudio/artifacts/2a7c5f08-d758-4a0e-bf87-d352fd259607/implementation_plan.md\n[AIS_METADATA_SECTION_END]"
    user_requests: "## **1. RAEC Analysis of Your FC 27 UT App Implementation Plan**\n\nAnchored to **Wednesday, October 21, 2026 (1:32 PM BST)** ($T = 0$)\342\200\224the final 24 hours of **EA Sports FC 27 Season 1** (which concludes tomorrow, Thursday, October 22, 2026) during the **2026/27 football season**\342\200\224your current Google AI Studio implementation plan lays a solid foundation for a cross-device companion app, but it misses several game-changing mechanics introduced in **EA Sports FC 27**.\n\n---\n\n### **A. Review & Audit: What is \"Based\" (Strong & Well-Designed)**\n\n* **Temporal & Roster Grounding ($T = 0$ Anti-Bias Pipeline):** Anchoring the app to `Europe/London` time with a live countdown to the **18:00 UK daily content drop** and cross-verifying 2026/27 transfers via **[FotMob](https://www.fotmob.com/en-GB/players/675088/rodri)** (such as confirming Rodri as a 30-year-old defensive midfielder at FC Barcelona rather than Manchester City) prevents the AI from hallucinating outdated squads.\n* **Inventory-First SBC Philosophy:** Prioritizing untradeable cards, SBC storage, and duplicate fodder from your club *before* recommending console transfer market purchases mirrors the best coin-saving logic of premium solvers like **[EasySBC](https://www.easysbc.io/get-sbc-solver)**.\n* **Dual-Viewport Ergonomics (Asus ZenBook UX482 + Mobile):** Splitting the navigation between a dense, multi-column desktop workspace (ideal for your ZenBook\'s main display and ScreenPad Plus secondary touchscreen) and a thumb-friendly mobile bottom navigation bar (**375px\342\200\223430px**) avoids the ad-heavy clutter that slows down traditional database sites.\n* **Hands-Free Voice Roster Sync (`gemini-3.5-transcribe`):** Dictating pack pulls or evolution progress out loud while holding your Xbox controller is a genuinely practical quality-of-life feature that removes the friction of typing player names mid-session.\n* **5% EA Tax & Net Profit Calculation:** Baking the mandatory **5% EA Transfer Market tax** directly into investment tracking ensures you never accidentally flip a card at a net coin loss.\n\n---\n\n### **B. Evaluate & Critique: Critical Flaws & Missing FC 27 Mechanics**\n\n| **Audit Area** | **What Your Current Plan Does** | **Why It Fails / What It Misses in Live EA FC 27 ($T = 0$)** |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| **1. The \"Gallery Grind\" Misinterpretation** | Treats \"Gallery Grind\" as repeatable upgrade SBC loops (e.g., 82+ Player Picks). | In **[EA Sports FC 27](https://www.ea.com/games/ea-sports-fc/fc-27/news/pitch-notes-fc27-fut-deep-dive)**, the **FUT Gallery** is a brand-new permanent collection system featuring **100+ Sets**, **Set Grades**, **Tags**, and an overall **Gallery Level**. Cards you pack or buy stay recorded in your Gallery even *after* you sell them or submit them into SBCs. Your plan completely lacks a **FUT Gallery Set & Tag Tracker**. |\n| **2. Outdated SBC Solver Logic** | Only builds traditional 11-player rating and chemistry combinations. | FC 27 introduced **Streamlined SBCs** for the majority of Player and Upgrade SBCs. Instead of building an 11-man squad with chemistry links, you submit eligible cards across multiple partial attempts to hit a target **Item Score**. Your solver *must* calculate **Cheapest Item Score per Coin** alongside traditional 11-player puzzle SBCs. |\n| **3. Missing Rarity Refresh & Holographic Cards** | Assumes legacy Common/Rare Gold splits. | FC 27 eliminated the Common/Rare split on base cards (they are now simply Bronze, Silver, or Gold) and introduced tradeable **Holographic Items**: **Regular Holographic** ($\\le 87$ OVR) and **Pristine Holographic** ($\\ge 88$ OVR). Holographic cards grant stacked bonus points toward both **Streamlined SBC Item Scores** and **Gallery Set Grades**. |\n| **4. Linear Evolution Assumptions** | Treats Evolutions as simple linear stat upgrades. | FC 27 introduced **Branching Evolution Pathways** (where you choose between diverging stat/PlayStyle branches at specific levels) and the recurring **PlayStyles Lab** (capped at **3 PlayStyles+** maximum in FC 27, with pre-applied PlayStyles). It also ignores the **31 Player Roles & Focuses** that dictate AI movement on the pitch. |\n| **5. Live Market Feed Bottleneck** | Relies solely on `googleSearch` grounding for live console transfer prices. | Think of `googleSearch` like sending a courier to read a newspaper\342\200\224it is great for checking who won a match or reading a promo list, but too slow and rate-limited for tracking 50 live auction prices every minute. You need a cached price-ingestion layer or MCP connector for console market data. |\n\n---\n\n### **C. Post-RAEC Action Plan: How to Improve, Enhance, Upgrade, Augment, Potentiate & Expand**\n\n* **Improve (Fix the SBC Engine):** Split the SBC module into a **Dual-Mode Solver**:\n1. **Streamlined SBC Item Score Calculator:** Ranks your club fodder and market cards by **Coins per Item Score Point**, accounting for Rating, Rarity, and **Holographic** multipliers.\n2. **Traditional Puzzle SBC Solver:** Uses a fast mathematical solver (Deterministic Linear Programming) for 11-player chemistry/rating puzzles rather than waiting 15 seconds for an LLM to guess combinations.\n\n\n* **Enhance (Build a True FUT Gallery Set & Tag Optimizer):** Add a dedicated **Gallery Grind Module** that tracks your progress across the 100+ permanent Gallery Sets (such as *Season 1 Combined Rarities: Ones to Watch, Destined for Glory, and Future Stars*), calculates **Tag Bonuses** (combinations of specific item types that multiply your Set Grade), and suggests \"Rent-and-Sell\" players you can buy on the console market, register into your Gallery Set, and immediately sell back.\n* **Upgrade (Branching Evolution Pathways & Role Fit):** Upgrade the Evolution Advisor to map **Branching Pathways** alongside **[FUT.GG](https://www.fut.gg/roles/)**-style **31 Roles & Focuses** (e.g., showing whether Branch A or Branch B turns your midfielder into a better *Box-to-Box++* vs. *Holding++*).\n* **Augment (ZenBook UX482 Dual-Screen Mode):** Add a toggleable **\"ScreenPad Plus Ticker Bar\"** layout specifically formatted for the secondary bottom touchscreen on your Asus ZenBook UX482, keeping your live Watchlist, 18:00 BST drop timer, and Streamlined SBC Item Score tally pinned on the bottom screen while the Squad Builder fills the main 14-inch display.\n* **Potentiate (Holographic Arbitrage Alerts):** Unlock hidden coin profits by flagging **Regular ($\\le 87$) and Pristine ($\\ge 88$) Holographic cards** listed on the console market near base special card prices\342\200\224either to flip for profit or to use as super-charged **Item Score** boosters in Streamlined SBCs.\n* **Expand (Season Ladder & SP Pacing Tracker):** Because FC 27 caps match-earned Season Points (SP) at **850 SP per day** (15\342\200\223100 SP per match) and features **Gauntlet / Live Events**, add a daily SP & Objective Stacker that tells you how to combine Foundations, Evolution tasks, and Live Events in the fewest matches possible.\n\n---\n\n## **2. Ecosystem Comparison: FUTBIN vs. FUT.GG vs. EasySBC vs. Your App**\n\n### **A. Feature & Architecture Comparison Matrix**\n\n| **Feature / Capability** | **[FUTBIN (FC 27)](https://www.futbin.com/whats-new-fc-27)** | **[FUT.GG (FC 27)](https://www.fut.gg/evo-lab/)** | **[EasySBC (FC 27)](https://www.google.com/search?q=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.easysbc.io%2Fmeta-rating)** | **Your FC 27 UT App (With RAEC Upgrades)** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **Primary Strength** | Console market prices, price graphs, & **[Gallery Builder](https://www.futbin.com/whats-new-fc-27)** | **[Evo Lab](https://www.fut.gg/evo-lab/)**, **[31 Roles & Focuses](https://www.fut.gg/roles/)**, & **[Best PlayStyles by Role](https://www.google.com/search?q=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.fut.gg%2Fplaystyles%2Fbest-by-role%2F)** | **[AI SBC Solver](https://www.easysbc.io/get-sbc-solver)** with Club Import & **[Meta Ratings](https://www.google.com/search?q=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.easysbc.io%2Fmeta-rating)** | **Unified Personal AI Terminal** combining Club Sync, Gallery Grind, Evo Lab & Market Alerts |\n| **Streamlined SBC (Item Score) Support** | Dedicated pages showing item score contributions | Dedicated **Streamlined SBC Solver** & Cheapest by Rating | Club-aware solver (Premium credit system) | **Club-First Item Score & Holographic Multiplier Optimizer** |\n| **Traditional 11-Player SBC Solutions** | Community-submitted squads (often price-fixed by traders) | Basic rating combination tables | Dynamic AI solver using your own untradeable club cards | **Deterministic Math Solver + Gemini Advisor** using your synced roster |\n| **Evolutions & Branching Pathways** | Good database, clunky chain builder | Industry gold standard (**Evo Lab** + PlayStyles Lab previews) | Evolution states scored by **Meta Rating** change | **Squad-Aware Evo Chainer** that checks chemistry & Role++ fit with your current XI |\n| **FUT Gallery Set & Tag Planning** | Full **Gallery Builder** with Set Grades & eligible cards | **FUT Gallery** & **Holographic Cards** database | Minimal Gallery focus | **Active Gallery Grind Planner** (\"Buy, Register in Set, Resell\" calculator) |\n| **Club Inventory Synchronization** | Manual / broken browser import | Manual tracking in **GG Club** | Chrome Extension Web App importer ($11.99/mo Ultimate tier for unlimited solves) | **1-Click Web App JSON + Google Drive Sync + Hands-Free Voice Input** |\n| **User Experience & Ad Load** | Heavy banner/video ads on desktop & mobile | Very clean, fast, modern dark UI | Clean web UI, but lacks a dedicated mobile app | **Zero Ads**, custom tailored for **Asus ZenBook UX482** & mobile bottom-bar |\n\n---\n\n### **B. Similarities, Differences, Pros & Cons Across the Big Three**\n\n| **Platform** | **Key Similarities to Your Vision** | **Key Differences** | **Pros** | **Cons** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **[FUTBIN](https://www.futbin.com/whats-new-fc-27)** | Dense desktop market terminal, live console prices, Squad Builder, and FC 27 Gallery Set tracking. | Relies on static community-built SBC squads rather than personalized club-inventory AI solving. | Largest historical price database; rapid updates at 18:00 BST content drops; built-in **Gallery Builder**. | Community SBC solutions get instantly price-fixed; intrusive ads slow down laptop/mobile browsers. |\n| **[FUT.GG](https://www.google.com/search?q=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.fut.gg%2Fcompare%2F)** | Deep focus on **Evolutions**, **PlayStyles**, **Roles++**, and clean mobile-friendly card comparisons. | Less focused on personal wallet management, coin flipping, or automated club inventory imports. | Best **Evo Lab** for previewing branching Pathways; pro-curated **[Best PlayStyles by Role](https://www.google.com/search?q=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.fut.gg%2Fplaystyles%2Fbest-by-role%2F)** guides. | Doesn\'t automatically cross-reference your personal untradeable fodder when suggesting squads. |\n| **[EasySBC](https://www.google.com/search?q=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.easysbc.io%2Fmeta-rating)** | AI-driven SBC solving using your imported club inventory and evaluating cards beyond face OVR. | Operates on a freemium credit paywall ($11.99/month for unlimited Ultimate solves) and lacks trading/Gallery tools. | **Meta Ratings** (S to D tiers) accurately reflect in-game performance (Pace, PlayStyles+, AcceleRATE, Role). | Web-only with no dedicated mobile app; extension occasionally fails to recognize owned cards without refreshing. |\n\n---\n\n## **3. Brainstorming & Ideating Additional Custom Features for Your App**\n\nTo make your app genuinely superior for your personal setup rather than just cloning FUTBIN, consider adding these six high-impact features to your implementation plan:\n\n1. **\"Gallery Rent-and-Flip\" Optimizer:**\n* Since **[EA FC 27\'s FUT Gallery](https://www.google.com/search?q=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.wslfootball.com%2Fnews%2Fultimate-team-in-ea-sports-fctm-27-whats-new)** permanently records a player in your Gallery Sets even if you immediately sell them or submit them into an SBC, this tool scans your incomplete Gallery Sets and identifies cards currently trading near their **Quick Sell (discard) floor** or minimum price range. You buy them on console, unlock the Gallery Set Grade and **Tag Bonus**, and flip them back on the market for near-zero net coin loss after the 5% tax.\n\n\n2. **Dual-Mode SBC Solver (Item Score + Chemistry Puzzle):**\n* Adds a toggle inside the SBC View between **Streamlined Mode** (optimizing rating + rarity + Holographic bonuses to hit target **Item Scores** using duplicate storage first) and **Puzzle Mode** (11-player chemistry solver).\n\n\n3. **Custom \"In-Game Meta Score\" Engine (Role++ & PlayStyle+ Weighted):**\n* Inspired by **[EasySBC Meta Ratings](https://www.google.com/search?q=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.easysbc.io%2Fmeta-rating)** and **[FUT.GG Roles](https://www.fut.gg/roles/)**, calculate a custom 1\342\200\223100 score for every card in every specific **Role** (e.g., *Inside Forward++* vs. *Poacher++*) based on FC 27\'s 3-PlayStyle+ cap, AcceleRATE type, Weak Foot/Skill Moves, and key sub-attributes (Agility, Balance, Composure, Reactions).\n\n\n4. **5G Connection-Aware Trading Mode:**\n* High-speed 59th-minute sniping requires ultra-low latency, which can fluctuate on a 5G home hub compared to FTTP fibre. Add a **\"Lazy Buyer / Bid Flipper\" Filter** to your Market View that focuses on **1-hour mass bidding**, **Out-of-Packs Campaign Flips** (like *Destined for Glory* or *Future Stars*), and  fodder cycling\342\200\224strategies where a 40ms ping spike won\'t cost you the trade.\n\n\n5. **Multi-Objective & Evolution \"Match Stacker\":**\n* With FC 27\'s daily **850 SP match cap**, **Foundations groups**, **Single-Player Live Events**, and **Branching Evolution objectives** (which often require specific appearances, goals, or assists across 9 daily attempts), the Match Stacker analyzes all your active objectives and generates a single starting XI that progresses **4 to 5 objectives simultaneously** in every match.\n\n\n6. **Gauntlet & Squad Foundations Builder:**\n* Borrow **[FUT.GG\'s Gauntlet Builder](https://www.fut.gg/roles/)** concept to help you build multi-squad rotations using your untradeable club depth without reusing locked players.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## **4. Agentic Workflow Assessment & Prototype Blueprint**\n\nIn software engineering, an **Agentic Workflow** is like hiring an autonomous research assistant who can check multiple sources, run calculations, verify its own work, and update your dashboard without you having to click five buttons. However, adding autonomous AI agents to *every* feature will slow down your app and burn through API quota (as seen in the `Quota limits exceeded` warnings in your AI Studio log).\n\n### **A. Scrupulous Audit: Where to Use an Agent vs. Deterministic Code**\n\n| **App Task / Module** | **Use Agentic Workflow?** | **Why / Latency & Resource Justification** |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| **Streamlined SBC Item Score & 11-Player Rating Math** | **NO (Use Standard Code)** | Adding numbers to hit an Item Score or 86 Squad Rating takes **2 milliseconds** in plain TypeScript math. Using an AI agent here wastes 10\342\200\22320 seconds of latency and burns paid API tokens. |\n| **UI Rendering, 5% EA Tax Calc & Clock ($T=0$)** | **NO (Use Standard Code)** | Instant, deterministic arithmetic. Zero benefit from AI reasoning. |\n| **18:00 BST Daily Content Drop, Evo Chain & Market Arbitrage Pipeline** | **YES (High Value Agentic Workflow)** | Every day at 18:00 UK time, EA drops new SBCs, Evolutions, and Promo cards. An autonomous multi-step workflow can ingest the new drop, cross-check your synced club inventory, simulate branching Evolution chains, and alert you to instant profit flips before the wider market reacts. |\n\n---\n\n### **B. Concise Blueprint: \"18:00 BST Daily Drop & Evo-Market Agent\"**\n\nDesigned for your **Google AI Studio (Paid Tier) + Antigravity 2.24 (with local MCP database connectors)** setup, this workflow runs only when triggered by a content drop or club import:\n\n1. **Step 1 \342\200\224 Ingestion & Grounding Node (`gemini-3.8-flash` + MCP Connector):**\n* **What it does:** At 18:00 BST ($T=0$), fetches the newly released FC 27 SBC requirements, new Evolution eligibility rules (e.g., max OVR, max PlayStyles+), and current console prices from your local MCP SQLite/Firestore cache.\n\n\n2. **Step 2 \342\200\224 Club Cross-Examination & Evolution Simulator (Deterministic Filter + `gemini-4-argon`):**\n* **What it does:** Filters your synced club inventory for eligible cards, simulates both branches of any new **Evolution Pathway**, and flags \"Hidden Gem\" links (e.g., an 82-rated card in your club that gains a *Role++* and links to FC Barcelona\'s Rodri).\n\n\n3. **Step 3 \342\200\224 Actionable Output & Workspace Logger:**\n* **What it does:** Pushes a 3-bullet \"Daily Action Card\" to your ZenBook dashboard (*1. Sell these 3 tradeable cards spiking from today\'s SBC; 2. Complete this Streamlined SBC using 4 duplicate untradeables; 3. Start this Evolution pathway*) and logs the price snapshot to Google Drive/Sheets.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## **5. Ready-to-Paste Revision Prompt for Google AI Studio**\n\nIf you want to upgrade the plan currently sitting on your screen, click **\"Revise...\"** in Google AI Studio and paste this exact prompt:\n\n> **Revision Instructions:**\n> Please update the implementation plan and architecture to reflect the real live mechanics of **EA Sports FC 27 Ultimate Team** (as of October 2026) and prevent API quota exhaustion:\n> 1. **Dual-Mode SBC Solver:** Support FC 27\'s new **Streamlined SBCs** (calculating Cheapest **Item Score** per coin using Rating, Rarity, and **Regular/Pristine Holographic** multipliers, plus partial submissions and duplicate storage) alongside traditional 11-player chemistry/rating SBCs. Use fast deterministic TypeScript math for the rating/score calculations and reserve Gemini API calls for high-level squad advice.\n> 2. **Authentic FUT Gallery Set & Tag Tracker:** Replace the mislabeled \"Gallery Grind\" description with FC 27\'s actual **FUT Gallery** system (tracking the 100+ permanent Sets, Set Grades, **Tag Bonuses**, and overall Gallery Level, plus a \"Rent-and-Sell\" calculator since cards stay recorded in Gallery Sets after being sold).\n> 3. **FC 27 Evolutions & Roles++:** Support **Branching Evolution Pathways**, the **PlayStyles Lab** (3 PlayStyles+ cap), and all **31 Player Roles & Focuses** accompanied by a custom **Meta Score (1\342\200\223100)** per Role.\n> 4. **Asus ZenBook UX482 ScreenPad Mode:** Add a compact secondary ticker view optimized for the ZenBook\'s dual-screen workflow alongside the mobile bottom navigation bar.\n> \n> \n\n---\n\n## **6. Computer Science & Technical Jargon Glossary**\n\n| **Technical Term / Jargon** | **Plain-English Definition & Everyday Analogy** |\n| --- | --- |\n| **Implementation Plan** | The architectural blueprint a coding assistant writes *before* building an app, listing every screen, database, and feature so you can approve or edit it first\342\200\224like an architect\'s floor plan before pouring concrete. |\n| **JSON (JavaScript Object Notation)** | A lightweight, standardized text format used to store and send structured data (like your list of FC 27 players, their ratings, and untradeable status) between websites and apps\342\200\224like a digital packing slip. |\n| **DOM Scraping / Web App Exporter** | A browser tool (like Paletools or EasySBC\'s Chrome Extension) that reads the player cards displayed on EA\'s official Web App screen and packages them into a file you can import elsewhere. |\n| **Deterministic Algorithm** | A standard math formula or code script that always produces the exact same answer instantly (like a pocket calculator), as opposed to an AI model that predicts words and takes several seconds to \"think.\" |\n| **Combinatorial Optimization** | Finding the cheapest or best group of items from thousands of possibilities that meet strict rules (e.g., picking 11 players from a 500-card club to hit an 86 rating and 31 chemistry for the lowest coin cost). |\n| **API Quota / Rate Limit** | A cap on how many requests your app can send to an AI model (like `gemini-4-argon`) per minute or per day. Exceeding it causes the `Quota limits exceeded` error visible in your AI Studio chat history. |\n| **OAuth (Open Authorization)** | The secure \"Sign in with Google\" handshake that lets your FC 27 app save backup files to your Google Drive without ever seeing or storing your actual password. |\n| **Firebase Firestore** | Google\'s cloud database that automatically syncs data in real time across devices\342\200\224so when you update your squad on your Asus ZenBook, it instantly updates on your phone screen. |\n| **Express Server (`server.ts`)** | The \"back office\" code of your web app that securely handles Gemini AI requests and database saves behind the scenes, keeping your API keys hidden from the public browser screen. |\n| **MCP (Model Context Protocol) Connector** | A universal plug-in standard that lets an AI assistant (like in Antigravity 2.24) securely read and write directly to your local databases, files, or external tools without custom glue code. |\n| **Responsive Viewport (`375px\342\200\223430px`)** | Designing a website\'s layout using tools like **Tailwind CSS** so it automatically rearranges itself from a wide multi-column desktop dashboard into a narrow, thumb-friendly phone screen (`375px` to `430px` wide). |\n| **Agentic Workflow** | A system where an AI doesn\'t just answer a single question, but autonomously executes a multi-step loop (e.g., *Search new SBC $\\rightarrow$ Check club inventory $\\rightarrow$ Calculate profit $\\rightarrow$ Send alert*). |\n\n---\n\nWould you like me to refine that **Revision Prompt** to prioritize any specific feature (such as the **FUT Gallery Rent-and-Flip Calculator** or the **ZenBook Dual-Screen Ticker**), or would you like to dive deeper into how to stop those `Gemini 4 Argon Quota limits exceeded` errors inside Google AI Studio?\n[AIS_METADATA_SECTION_START]\nPlan action: revise\nPlan path: .aistudio/artifacts/2a7c5f08-d758-4a0e-bf87-d352fd259607/implementation_plan.md\nInstructions: If you need more context from the user you must first ask the user some questions using the ask_question tool. If you ask questions, you must wait for the user\'s answers. After the questions you must present a plan.\n[AIS_METADATA_SECTION_END]"
    user_requests: "i need you to be able to instantaneously and dynamically track player prices and new items added to the game. \n\ni would also like you to break it down into 2 principle domains: Menus & Gameplay. of Course the gameplay section gives tips on meta formations at the time of prompting or your answer. it will include tactics, player roles, player profiles, chemistry styles, playstyles, stats in isolation & when synthesised. you will be able to calculate additive effects of stats, playstyles, chemistry styles, acceleration type, chemistry, player body type. make sure to keep up to date with software and firmware patches as the mechanics of the game change dynamically with patches throughout the year principally altering gameplay mechanics. \n\nDesign and implement real-time market data visualization for the EA Sports FC 27 Ultimate Team assistant app. Include interactive charts for player prices, market trends, and historical data. Ensure the data is specific to EA Sports FC 27 Ultimate Team console and optimized for mobile screen resolutions. Integrate Gemini API to analyze these trends and provide actionable insights.\n[AIS_METADATA_SECTION_START]\nPlan action: revise\nPlan path: .aistudio/artifacts/2a7c5f08-d758-4a0e-bf87-d352fd259607/implementation_plan.md\nInstructions: If you need more context from the user you must first ask the user some questions using the ask_question tool. If you ask questions, you must wait for the user\'s answers. After the questions you must present a plan.\n[AIS_METADATA_SECTION_END]"
    user_requests: "what mcp\'s should we add. use futbin as a resource\n[AIS_METADATA_SECTION_START]\nPlan action: revise\nPlan path: .aistudio/artifacts/2a7c5f08-d758-4a0e-bf87-d352fd259607/implementation_plan.md\nInstructions: If you need more context from the user you must first ask the user some questions using the ask_question tool. If you ask questions, you must wait for the user\'s answers. After the questions you must present a plan.\n[AIS_METADATA_SECTION_END]"
    user_requests: "antigravity 2.25 is the latest and current version as of todays date and time. the app must be orchestrated and built by antigravity 2.25 desktop app. but there needs to be dynamic temporal anchoring to every interaction with the app and to every runtime and thing the app does. this also includes finding out what the latest and therefore current features of that firmware version of antigravity 2.0 desktop app.\n[AIS_METADATA_SECTION_START]\nPlan action: revise\nPlan path: .aistudio/artifacts/2a7c5f08-d758-4a0e-bf87-d352fd259607/implementation_plan.md\nInstructions: If you need more context from the user you must first ask the user some questions using the ask_question tool. If you ask questions, you must wait for the user\'s answers. After the questions you must present a plan.\n[AIS_METADATA_SECTION_END]"
    user_requests: "this means new features and additions to the app based on antigravity 2.0 desktop app software updates and thus new features and capabilities. \n\nTherefore, we use dynamic temporal anchoring to work out the exact date and time of my prompt or my interaction and then any runtime that\'s initiated in the app.\n\nThis can be used to find the latest and current firmware version or software version of the app.\n\nFor example, right now as of 23rd of October 2026 at 7:35 a.m., the latest and current version is Anti-Gravity 2.25 desktop app.\n[AIS_METADATA_SECTION_START]\nPlan action: revise\nPlan path: .aistudio/artifacts/2a7c5f08-d758-4a0e-bf87-d352fd259607/implementation_plan.md\nInstructions: If you need more context from the user you must first ask the user some questions using the ask_question tool. If you ask questions, you must wait for the user\'s answers. After the questions you must present a plan.\n[AIS_METADATA_SECTION_END]"
    user_requests: "Proceed\n[AIS_METADATA_SECTION_START]\nPlan action: proceed\nPlan path: .aistudio/artifacts/2a7c5f08-d758-4a0e-bf87-d352fd259607/implementation_plan.md\n[AIS_METADATA_SECTION_END]"
