  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Assessing System Skills**\n\nI\'m now focusing on assessing the functional, API, and persistence skills within planning mode. Currently I am looking to improve the `planning-mode` skills, as a component of `system_skills`. My goal is to determine the scope for enhancement to the API and persistence aspects.\n\n\n**Designing Smart Model Tiers**\n\nI\'m now designing a 5-Tier Cost, Latency & Benchmark Smart Model. My current focus is integrating the `gemini-api`, `firebase-integration-rpc`, and `workspace-integration` skills, specifically considering the confirmed answers. I\'m taking into account the user\'s focus on auto-routing by task complexity with manual override, as well as displaying model tier, latency, and reason.\n\n\n**Defining Auto-Routing Tiers**\n\nI\'m currently defining the auto-routing tiers for our revised `implementation_plan.md`. I am implementing a deterministic local engine (Tier 0) and evaluating the integration of `gemini-3.1-flash-lite` (Tier 1) for higher-frequency, lower-complexity tasks. I\'m taking cost and latency into account, specifically for arithmetic and mechanic lookups within the deterministic engine.\n\n\n**Evaluating Tier Benchmarks**\n\nI\'m now evaluating Tier 2\'s characteristics, specifically its performance on real-time web grounding and fact verification. The goal is to evaluate if `gemini-3.8-flash` with `googleSearch` can perform the desired actions at the given latency and cost benchmarks. The benchmarks I\'m looking at are an unverified **EA Sports FC 27 Xbox Series S** Buy-Now price on FUTBIN Console and **Antigravity `v2.25`** patch notes.\n\n\n**Defining Reasoning Tiers**\n\nI am now defining the new specialized audio and high-reasoning tiers. I plan to invoke `gemini-4-argon` for complex strategic optimizations and `Antigravity` UI synthesis, specifically for multi-branch trade-offs within a budget. I will also incorporate `gemini-3.5-transcribe` when receiving controller voice updates. These tiers are selected to balance high performance and cost effectiveness.\n\n\n"
